RM – Comics reader
Reader with customization for manga and comics, and with downloads
RM is a simple reader for manga, comics and PDF files with a wide range of settings! In addition, it has a built-in ability to download chapters from supported sites.
RM can open ZIP, RAR, 7Z* with image files (a popular format on websites), ComicBook archives, TXT files (if you suddenly want to read non-comics), and PDF files*!
* - Unfortunately, support for 7Z, CB7 and PDF files is disabled on Android < 5.0 :(
The application has many features that improve the reading experience:
📁 Creating titles (folders): each added chapter can be distributed between folders to quickly find the required chapter, and for “endless” reading;
⏬ Downloading chapters and titles from the Internet: when adding a title/chapter, you can use downloading from supported sites, directly from the application;
🔗 Sorting the order of titles and chapters: the application has a mode for editing lists, which helps you fine-tune the order of everything you need;
📚 Reader with huge customisation: a huge number of settings makes possible to customise everything finely and as conveniently as possible;
🔍 Zoom for pages: in addition to the reader, there is a page zoom using gestures, so that not a single letter will go unnoticed;
✂️ Ad filter in titles: you can set up an ad filter that will remove ads of all sites from the title completely automatically, saving a lot of time;
🖥️ Fullscreen mode: the reader has a fullscreen mode function - nothing will interfere with reading!
In addition, RM...
📱 Has a convenient and beautiful design (just like system applications);
💬 Translated into English, Russian, Ukrainian, Belarusian (there will be more in the future);
🔨 Supported on devices starting from Android 4.0 (such a wide selection of phones, yes);
💾 Works with SD cards (if you have one);
🛄 Uses some system functions that, for some reason, are not used by other applications;
To download chapters from the Internet, you need to...
1. Add a title from the internet using the search bar in the application;
...or...
1. Add a link to a supported site to any title;
2. Open required title;
3. Click the button in the lower right corner;
4. Download chapters from the list;
Done!
To use the application you need...
1. Download any suitable file (preferably with the required content);
2. Open the application and select any title;
3. Click on the button in the lower right corner;
4. Select the downloaded file and enter information about the chapter;
5. Read and enjoy :)
